  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Adds OpenReadRangeAsync to IShelfClient, in the HTTP client and the in-memory one: it reads part of a file, from an offset for a length or to the end, as a ShelfFileRange carrying the range's offset and length, the file's total length and the SHA-256 of the contents it came from, to seek in a video or answer a browser's Range request. A range starting at or past the end is refused with range_not_satisfiable; given the SHA-256 read earlier, a file whose contents have changed is refused with content_changed. Only a range that is the whole file is checked against its SHA-256. Works with ByteShelf server 2.0.0 and later. IShelfClient gains a member, so an implementation outside ByteShelfClient must add it. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/byte-shelf/blob/client-v2.2.0/ByteShelfClient/README.md",
